    "prose": "Thunder cracked over the lighthouse, and rain hammered the walls. The hatchling flinched against its mother.\n\nThe sea dragon turned toward it. Her broad body swung away from the nest approach, leaving a brief opening.\n\nEkin rushed through the open approach.\n\n“Ekin, wait!” Duru shouted.\n\nEkin reached for the brass compass. Duru saw her hand stretch toward it.\n\nThe hatchling squealed and sprang away. It scrambled down the narrow internal stair to the dry stair section. Ekin jerked around and saw it flee below her. The hatchling kept going down the lower stair and reached the lower room’s dry ledge.\n\nThe mother whipped back defensively. Her body struck the nest, and the compass spun across the floor. It bounced onto the turning stair as a wave crashed against the lighthouse.\n\nWater burst through the fixed sea-facing grate below. The lower room began to flood, and the rising wash caught the compass. Ekin watched the brass circle tumble through the lower room, flash once in the gray daylight, and wash through the iron grate into the sea.\n\n“No!” Her cry vanished beneath the storm.\n\nThe mother charged after her hatchling, but she could not descend the narrow stair. Her shoulders met the walls at the turn. She pulled back and tried again, twisting her body, yet the tight bend stopped her. Ekin saw her remain trapped in the upper room, staring down toward the stranded hatchling.\n\nAnother surge foamed across the lower room. The little dragon pressed itself against the dry ledge above the floodwater.\n\nEkin descended the narrow internal stair to the dry section.\n\nDuru followed down the same stair and reached the dry section beside her.\n\nNeither girl entered the water. Ekin stared past the frightened hatchling at the grate where the compass had vanished. Her outstretched hand still trembled.\n\n“I caused this,” she whispered.\n\nDuru looked at the rising water below, then at Ekin. “We can’t get the compass back.”\n\nEkin swallowed hard. This time, she did not argue.",
